        skos:definition        "A British Geological Survey-built airgun profiling system composed of: a Bolt 600B gun array of five guns as sound source, each fitted with 655 cm^3 (i.e. 40 cubic inches) firing chambers; a hydrophone streamer; a compressor container; a BGS/CODA digital acquisition and processing system; and a Waverley thermal recorder."@en;
