<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1518/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1518";
        dc:date                "2024-08-19 14:03:59.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1518";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-08-19 14:03:59.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1518/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1518/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "Young 85000";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/101/>;
        skos:definition        "A 2-axis, no-moving-parts wind sensor. It is ideal for general meteorological applications requiring accurate and reliable measurement. Measurement results are available as calibrated voltage output signals or serial data using RS-232, RS-485, or SDI-12 connections. Serial formats may be selected for direct connection to Young Wind Tracker displays, marine NMEA systems, SDI-12 data loggers, and ASCII serial communication programs. The sensor measures wind based on the transit time of ultrasonic pulses between four transducers. Air flow alters the transit time which is used to calculate flow velocity. Wind direction is determined from relative velocities along each acoustic path. The sensor is constructed using UV-stabilised thermoplastic, stainless steel, and anodised aluminium for superior environmental resistance. It is easily mounted on standard 1 inch (IPS) pipe. An orientation ring preserves mounting position when the sensor is removed. Continuous output or polled operation may be used. WIND SPEED; Range: 0 - 70 m/s (156 mph), Resolution: 0.1 m/s, Accuracy: 0 to 30 m/s, +/- 2 % or 0.1 m/s, 30 to 70 m/s, +/- 3 %. WIND DIRECTION; Azimuth Range: 0 - 360 degrees, Resolution: 1 degree, Accuracy: +/- 2 degrees."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1518";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "R.M. Young 85000 ultrasonic anemometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00402/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0037/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0001/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::NETT0001";
        dc:date                "2012-05-11 10:27:07.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::NETT0001";
        pav:authoredOn         "2012-05-11 10:27:07.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0001/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0001/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "Adriatic plankton sampler";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/22/>;
        skos:definition        "Construction is a 50 cm diameter cylindrical sampler sent to depth with the cylinder net (0.25 mm mesh) closed and upside down (cod-end facing upward). A messenger releases the bottom margin of cylinder allowing it to drop open (115 cm length) and at the same time closing half circle doors. A second messenger releases the first support bridle and the sampler turns right side up. Sampler collects about 250 litres of water [Wiebe and Benfield 2003 Plate 11 A]."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::NETT0001";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Adriatic plankton sampler - Krsinic (1990)"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0020/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::NETT0020";
        dc:date                "2011-10-21 14:18:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::NETT0020";
        pav:authoredOn         "2011-10-21 14:18:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0020/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Clarke Jet Net HSS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/67/>;
        skos:definition        "Construction is a 12 cm diameter mouth opening with an overall length of 125 cm. Uses nylon netting with 0.44 mm mesh. Towing speeds up to 10.5 knots [Wiebe and Benfield 2003 Plate 18 E]."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::NETT0020";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Clarke Jet Net high-speed plankton sampler - Clarke (1964)"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1334/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1334";
        dc:date                "2024-08-01 14:12:24.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1334";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-08-01 14:12:24.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1334/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1334/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "Satlantic HyperSAS radiometer";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/304/>;
        skos:definition        "An above-water optical sensing system designed to provide continuous ocean colour measurements over the spectral range 350-800 nm. The HyperSAS can be mounted on ships and fixed platforms, or on aircrafts for remote sensing surveys. The standard configuration of the system includes one irradiance sensor to measure downwelling irradiance, and two hyperspectral radiance sensors to capture the sea surface signal. The irradiance sensor response is proportional to the cosine of the angle of incidence of the incoming radiation, while each radiance sensor has a 3 deg field of view (FOV). The orientation precision, geo-referencing and time-stamp accuracy may be improved by mounting an optional GPS unit with Satlantic tilt and heading sensor. Moreover, a radiation pyrometer may also be added to measure land or sea surface temperature."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1334";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Satlantic Hyperspectral Surface Acquisition System (HyperSAS) radiometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00226/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0027/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2157/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2157";
        dc:date                "2025-05-06 14:04:35.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2157";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-06 14:04:35.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2157/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Agilent 5110 ICP-OES";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB16/>;
        skos:definition        "The Agilent 5110 is an inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer. It is available in three configurations, synchronous vertical dual view (SVDV), vertical dual view, and radial view. It has a dichroic spectral combiner which allows it to use under 30 l of argon per sample. It measures all wavelengths in one and the SVDV version requires only one measurement per sample. The Agilent 5110 has a readback stability over 4 hours of near 100 % for over 10 elements in a 25 % NaCl solution, with a relative standard deviation under 1.3 %. Operating conditions altitude 0-3000 m, 15-30 deg C, 20-80 % relative humidity."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2157";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Agilent 5110 inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00548/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0042/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1112/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1112";
        dc:date                "2017-02-13 10:52:07.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1112";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-02-13 10:52:07.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1112/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1112/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "LDEO OBS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/368/>;
        skos:definition        "Ocean bottom seismometer instruments designed by the Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory (LDEO). Seismometer sensors are either a L4C 1 Hz geophone and a differential pressure gauge or a Trillium Compact seismometer, a Paroscientific absolute pressure gauge, and a hydrophone.  They can be deployed for depths up to 1000 m or 5000 m. They can be deployed for a maximum duration of 400 days."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1112";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory ocean bottom seismometer series"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00129/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0599/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0599";
        dc:date                "2013-02-07 15:47:04.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0599";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-02-07 15:47:04.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0599/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "POL 250kHz ADCP";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/115/>;
        skos:definition        "An ADCP with a range of 100 m, designed to measure currents in up to 24 bins. Data from bins in the shallowest 25 percent of the depth range (ie: closest to the transducer) and in the deepest 10 percent (furthest from the transducer) are unreliable due to interference. The instrument uses two orthogonal beams and a built-in compass to resolve northward and eastward components of current."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0599";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Proudman Oceanographic Laboratory 250kHz ADCP"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00003/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1949/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1949";
        dc:date                "2023-06-08 15:58:37.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1949";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-06-08 15:58:37.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1949/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Panasonic BB-HCM580";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/311/>;
        skos:definition        "An indoor monitoring camera with applications in monitoring large areas owing to its 360deg pan and 158deg tilt functionality. The HCM580 features 42 x power zoom (comprising 21 x optical and 2 x digital) and power over Ethernet (PoE), supporting use in remote areas and enabling control of the camera system over the internet. Sensor is a 1/4\" charge-coupled device (CCD) with approximately 320,000 pixels, resulting in a video quality of up to 640 x 480p and a maximum framerate of 30 fps. Has a colour night view mode to automatically adjust image brightness. Motion detection functionality enables images to be captured automatically and stored temporarily on the camera or sent via FTP data transfer or email. The camera can simultaneously send MPEG-4 images in three resolutions (VGA, QVGA and SCIF), in addition to JPEG images with the same resolutions. Can be paired with a glass dome housing to facilitate outside use."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1949";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Panasonic BB-HCM580 camera"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0258/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG01154/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1708/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1708";
        dc:date                "2021-06-23 15:58:21.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1708";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-06-23 15:58:21.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1708/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "HCMR Seismic Reflection System";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/153/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/369/>;
        skos:definition        "A single-channel seismic reflection profiling system used by HCMR. The system uses a Teledyne Bolt airgun at 1/10/ 40 cubic inches volume, and an SIG hydrophone streamer. The 65m active length single-channel streamer consists of 45 hydrophone elements at 1m spacing."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1708";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Hellenic Centre for Marine Research Single-Channel Airgun Seismic Reflection System"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG01016/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0181/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0421/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0421";
        dc:date                "2011-09-03 16:28:15.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0421";
        pav:authoredOn         "2011-09-03 16:28:15.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0421/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Varian 820-MS ICPMS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB15/>;
        skos:definition        "A compact, floor-mounted inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) featuring 90 deg reflecting ion optics systems for gigahertz sensitivity (1000 Mc/s/mg/L) and low background and interferences. The instrument comprises a sample introduction system (spraychamber, nebuliser and peristaltic pump), solid state 27 MHz RF generator and Turner Interlaced Coils. Plasma positioning, the triple stage vacuum system (which is fully contained within the instrument), all plasma gas flows, the mass analyzer and the Discrete Dynode Electron Multiplier (DDEM) detector are fully controlled by a PC. The DDEM detector provides nine decades of dynamic range in an all-digital pulse design. The Varian 820-MS system also features a unique Collision Reaction Interface (CRI) providing fast, flexible, interference-free analysis using simple collision and reaction gases. The instrument was originally manufactured by Varian, Inc., which was bought by Agilent Technologies in 2010."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0421";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Varian 820-MS  inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00548/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2189/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2189";
        dc:date                "2025-07-24 11:54:48.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2189";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-07-24 11:54:48.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2189/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Agilent 8800 QQQ ICP-MS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB15/>;
        skos:definition        "The Agilent 8800 is a triple quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer. It contains two quadrupole mass spectrometers (MS/MS) in tandem which are separated by the octopole reaction system 3 (ORS3) collision cell which uses an octopole ion guide. The first quadrupole prevents all off-mass ions from entering the cell, ensuring consistent and controlled interference removal in reaction mode. The instrument in reaction mode can use either On-Mass Mode, where reactive interferences are removed to allow an unreactive analyte to be measured at its original mass; or Mass-Shift Mode, where the reactive analyte is moved to a new mass free from the original interference. The MS/MS enables low level analysis of difficult elements such as S, P and Cl, and provides an abundance sensitivity of <10^-10."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2189";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Agilent 8800 triple quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00548/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0042/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2138/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2138";
        dc:date                "2025-02-14 11:24:53.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2138";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-02-14 11:24:53.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2138/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Thermo Scientific iCAP TQ ICP-MS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB15/>;
        skos:definition        "A benchtop triple quadrupole (TQ) inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) with a four channel peristaltic pump, three plasma gas flow controllers, and four QCell mass flow controllers. The iCAP TQ utilises triple quadrupole technology which allows the analyte signal to be isolated from interferences, enabling the analysis of complex or high-matrix samples. The high frequency (4 MHz) quadrupole mass analyser has pre and post filters for isolation of wanted ions. The instrument features Peltier cooled high purity quartz or perfluoroalkoxy alkane (PFA), and low volume, baffled cyclonic or double pass spray chambers to efficiently filter out larger aerosol droplets for improved plasma stability. A reaction finder method development assistant aids easy method development. The plasma system is designed to rapidly adapt to changing matrices and provide robustness for challenging samples such as highly volatile organic solvents. The argon ICP ion source has a digital, solid state radiofrequency generator, and dynamic frequency impedance matching the plasma at 27 MHz. The iCAP TQ has applications in trace element analysis of solid or liquid (particularly sediment or sea water) samples. It has a nebuliser default flow rate of 400 uL/min."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2138";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Thermo Fisher Scientific iCAP TQ inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00458/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0035/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2323/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2323";
        dc:date                "2026-08-11 08:56:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2323";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-08-11 08:56:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2323/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Agilent 7700 ICP-MS series";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB15/>;
        skos:definition        "A series of compact benchtop quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometers (ICP-MS) for multi-element analysis in complex sample matrices. Instruments feature a low-flow Peltier cooled sample introduction system, a fast, frequency-matching RF generator, and an off-axis ion lens. A 3rd generation Octopole Reaction System (ORS3) consisting of a temperature-controlled collision/reaction cell with a low internal volume acts to improve ion focussing and to increase collision efficiency. Other features include an octopole ion guide, a hyperbolic quadropole, and a dual mode electron multiplier detector that can provide 9 orders of dynamic range under standard operating conditions. Instruments can be operated in He mode for higher sensitivity, lower backgrounds, and more effective interference removal. A High Matrix Introduction (HMI) kit is available to allow the direct analysis of samples with high dissolved solids content, and a range of sample delivery systems and accessories are available as optional extras. Instruments can be linked to other systems to act as elemental detectors for separation technologies such as high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) or gas chromatography (GC) systems. Instruments within this series include the 7700x high-throughput instrument, the 7700s instrument for the analysis of high-purity materials, and the 7700e system for routine analysis."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2323";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Agilent 7700 inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer series"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00548/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0042/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1221/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1221";
        dc:date                "2024-08-21 16:29:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1221";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-08-21 16:29:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1221/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1221/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "Thermo Scientific Element XR HR-ICP-MS";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB15/>;
        skos:definition        "A high-resolution (HR) inductively coupled plasma (ICP) mass spectrometer (MS) composed of a dual mode secondary electron multiplier (SEM) and a Faraday detector. The ELEMENT XR instrument has a dynamic range of 5 x 10^7 to 1 x 10^12 counts per second (cps), and allows simultaneous measurement of elements at concentrations over 1000 ug/g."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1221";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Thermo Fisher Scientific ELEMENT XR high resolution inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00458/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2183/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2183";
        dc:date                "2025-07-09 11:21:21.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2183";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-07-09 11:21:21.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2183/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Mirion Alpha Analyst";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB53/>;
        skos:definition        "An alpha spectrometer designed for high-resolution analysis of alpha-emitting radionuclides and used for environmental monitoring, nuclear research and forensics, and healthcare assessments. The instrument has a modular design and can accomodate up to 6 Dual Spectrometer modules with Passivated Implanted Planar Silicon (PIPS) detectors and two vacuum chambers per module. The interactions as alpha particles from the sample strike the semiconductor material produce charge pulses which are proportional to the energy of the alpha particles. The pulses are converted to voltage and seen as peaks in the associated software. The instrument features automatic recoil suppression control, a clean vent port to reduce moisture and contamination buildup in chambers, a manual emergency venting valve, and Apex Alpha software for complete computer control. A range of detector sizes are available up to a maximum of 1200 mm squared. Based on use with a 450-18AM PIPS detector and a good quality Americium-241 point source: energy resolution <18 keV (full width at half maximum, FWHM) with a detector-source spacing equal to the detector diameter, detector efficiency >25% for detector-source spacing of less than 1 mm, and background < 1 count/hr above 3 MeV."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2183";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Mirion Alpha Analyst integrated alpha spectrometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG02110/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0341/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0210/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::NETT0210";
        dc:date                "2024-04-19 15:58:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::NETT0210";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-04-19 15:58:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0210/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
