        skos:definition        "The Knudsen 320M is an echosounder designed for water depths between 10 and 5000 m.  Using either the high (250kHz) or low (3.5kHz) frequency channels, or both simultaneously, the 320M produces a high resolution record depicting bottom profiles and sediment layers with 32 shades of grey"@en;
